# This file lists the 'plug-ins' with any arguments to be loaded by
# matchbox-desktop.
#
# It can be overridden on a per-user basis by copying this file to ~/.matchbox/
# and editing.

@MBDESKTOP_PLUGIN_DIR@/dotdesktop.so
# @MBDESKTOP_PLUGIN_DIR@/simplefilebrowser.so /

# tasks.so is deliberately NOT loaded. It adds an "Active Tasks" folder to
# the desktop, which is how Matchbox 0.9 exposed running applications
# before there was anywhere better to put them. On piko there is: the
# panel's mb-applet-tasks taskbar shows one button per running app, with
# its icon and name, permanently visible and one tap away -- so the folder
# is a second, worse copy of the same list that also costs a top-level
# desktop icon. The module is still built and installed; adding the line
# back here is all it takes to bring the folder back.
